@bank all
// SW2, 0.92.6 item 9, the cheap fix (the user: yes): any appointment you make with someone plays one of their own
// "Talk a while" talks when you're both sat down (talkpack/<id>.talk, their talk.start / talk.sit / talk.end frames).
// These are the few shared lines around it, said by whoever you meet, for the moments the talk frames don't cover.
// Voice tokens make them sound like the speaker. FX22: the keys, read as LINES['appt.<what>'].
//   appt.arrive   they arrive and sit with you (before their talk.start).
//   appt.wait     you arrive and they're already there.
//   appt.late     you arrive late (kind; never a guilt trip).
//   appt.notalk   for anyone with no talk pack: a short chat line, then appt.bye.
//   appt.bye      the appointment's time is up.

== appt.arrive
- {hi}. Right, I'm here. All yours.
- {hi}, {nick}. Sorry, the lift was full.
- There you are. I saved you a seat. Well, I sat near one.   #funny
- {hi}. I've been looking forward to this, honestly.   #warm
== appt.wait
- {hi}. You found it, then. Sit down.
- I was early. I'm never early. Don't get used to it.   #funny
- {hi}, {nick}. Sit. I've got ten minutes before anyone needs me.
== appt.late
- There you are. I was about to send the Watch out.   #funny
- No harm done. Sit. I've only just got comfy.
- {hi}. Late's fine. Here's better than not at all.   #warm
== appt.notalk
- So. How's it going, really? The board treating you all right?
- Tell me one good thing about your week. Just one.
- I like this. Sitting still. We should do it more.   #warm
== appt.bye
- Right, that's me. Same again some time?
- {bye}. Thanks for this. I mean it.   #warm
- Time's up, I'm afraid. The ship calls. {bye}.
